  %% --- the failure this graph exists to catch ---
  %% The shipped `requires` graph is acyclic and every edge resolves. The two
  %% quieter failures dependencyHealth() reports are (a) a `requires` id that no
  %% technique defines, and (b) a cycle, where "add oversight to the training
  %% loop" and "add training to the oversight loop" both look reasonable in
  %% isolation. Neither is drawn here because neither exists in the dataset.

  gap["dependencyHealth() audits the `requires` and<br/>`supersedes` edges. On the shipped data it reports<br/>no dangling ids and no cycles — and that is the<br/>result worth guarding, not an accident worth baking in."]

  gap -.-> t11
